21. Escaping Special Characters

Confluence Wiki Markup uses characters such as:

- "*"
- "_"
- "-"
- "+"
- "{"
- "}"
- "["
- "]"
- "|"
- "#"

When text containing these characters is incorrectly interpreted as formatting, use one of these approaches:

1. Wrap short technical text in inline code:

{noformat}
{{value_with_underscores}}
{noformat}

2. Put multiline technical text inside "{noformat}" or "{code}".

3. Escape the character with a backslash when supported:

{noformat}
*not bold*
{noformat}

For technical content, inline code or no-format blocks are usually safer than manual escaping.

